# Folder Organization

Keep the repository split by concern: datasets, reusable pipeline code, and exploratory work.

```
tcc/
├── data/
│   ├── raw/
│   │   ├── training/   # train_FD00x.txt (run-to-failure)
│   │   ├── test/       # test_FD00x.txt (truncated trajectories)
│   │   └── result/     # RUL_FD00x.txt (test ground-truth RUL)
│   └── processed/      # Cleaned / engineered artifacts only
├── notebooks/          # Ad-hoc exploratory Jupyter notebooks
├── src/                # Reusable pipeline modules + main experiment notebook
├── readme.md
└── .gitignore
```

## Placement Rules

- **`data/raw/`** — Original C-MAPSS files only. Do not overwrite or write pipeline outputs here. Keep the `training/`, `test/`, and `result/` split.
- **`data/processed/`** — Intermediate or derived artifacts from preprocessing/feature engineering. Never put raw NASA downloads here.
- **`src/`** — Production pipeline code, one responsibility per module:
  - `data.py` — load, clean, prepare tables
  - `features.py` — scaling, feature selection, sliding windows
  - `models.py` — LSTM/BiLSTM build, tuning, training, evaluation
  - `comparacao_final.ipynb` — end-to-end LSTM vs BiLSTM comparison (lives in `src/`, not `notebooks/`)
- **`notebooks/`** — Exploratory / experimental notebooks only. Do not put reusable helpers here; extract them into `src/`.

## Do / Don't

- ✅ Load from `data/raw/` → transform via `src/` → write derived outputs to `data/processed/`
- ✅ Add new reusable functions to the matching `src/*.py` module
- ✅ Put scratch analysis in `notebooks/`
- ❌ Mix raw and processed data in the same folder
- ❌ Duplicate pipeline logic inside notebooks when it belongs in `src/`
- ❌ Commit `data/` contents or `__pycache__/` (they are gitignored)
